                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \supsetneq
          %p
            We now have multiple meanings for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
            if one or both of these is already a rational number or a real number, but it is a theorem that the meanings are all consistent. We also have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty \leq x \leq \infty
            for every extended number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi x
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty \lt x \lt \infty
            for every bounded number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y
            or
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
          %p
            Each version of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partial order
            and each version of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasiorder"} quasiorder
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} total order
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt
            is the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+total+order"} strict total order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comparison"} comparison
            law for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt
            is invalid, which is why one-sided reals are not as well behaved as ordinary (located)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          %h2#suprema_and_infima Suprema and infima
          %p
            Given any collection of extended lower reals, their
            %strong supremum
            is an extended lower real which is found by taking the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            of lower sets. The supremum of an inhabited set of lower reals is a lower real, and the supremum of an inhabited set of bounded lower reals is bounded iff the set has a bounded lower real as an upper bound. In any case, this supremum really is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum"} supremum
            under
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
          %p
            Given any collection of extended upper reals, their
            %strong infimum
            is an extended upper real which is found by taking the union of upper sets. The infimum of an inhabited set of upper reals is an upper real, and the infimum of an inhabited set of bounded upper reals is bounded iff the set has a bounded upper real as a lower bound. In any case, this infimum really is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infimum"} infimum
            under
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
            of an intersection. (This construction makes sense even in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative
            constructive mathematics, though the adjoint functor theorem does not.) However, these may not be what we really want; an obvious example of this is if we take the infimum of a set of lower reals that happen to all be located, in which case what we really want is the corresponding
            %em upper
            real infimum (for instance, when defining
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/located+subspaces"} located subspaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MacNeille+real+numbers"} MacNeille real numbers
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inferior+limit"} inferior limit
            is …
          %h2#arithmetic Arithmetic
          %p
            In general, you can extend
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order-preserving+functions"} order-preserving functions
            of rational numbers to lower reals and to upper reals; you simply take the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of the lower or upper set and close it downward or upwards, as appropriate. If you have an order-reversing function of rational numbers, then you can apply it to a lower real to get an upper real and conversely; this is about the only interaction that I know of between the two kinds of one-sided real.
          %p
            Since addition is order-preserving, it works nicely, at least to make a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtraction"} subtraction
            doesn't work in general. Multiplication has trouble with negative numbers but produces good results if you restrict to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,\infty]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \cdot \infty = 0
            with lower reals but
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \cdot \infty = \infty
            with extended upper reals; thus,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {[{0,\infty}[}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
            for either lower or upper reals, while
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,\infty]
            is a rig only for lower reals. (This doesn't so much mean that upper reals behave worse than lower reals, as that extended reals on either side behave worse.) We can also use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithms"} logarithms
            to translate between addition and multiplication. (In particular,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo +
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty + \infty = -\infty
            with extended lower reals but
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo +
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty + \infty = \infty
            with extended upper reals.)
          %p
            Of course, arithmetic with one-sided real numbers is much easier than this in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ±
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm\infty
            may differ. Accordingly, the conventions for arithmetic with infinities can signal which sort of number is appropriate for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive
            development.
          %p
            If you want to do arbitrary arithmetic operations constructively on something more general than
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/located+real+numbers"} located real numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MacNeille+real+number"} MacNeille reals
          %h2#topology Topology
          %p
            Let's put this on a separate page:
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicontinuous+topology"} semicontinuous topology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
          %h2#in_topos_theory In topos theory
          %p
            There is a bijective correspondence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            extended lower real numbers in a sheaf topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sh}(X)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicontinuous+map"} lower semicontinuous
            functions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbb{R} \cup \{ +\infty \}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbb{R} \cup \{ +\infty \}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lower+semicontinuous+topology"} lower semicontinuous topology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(\mathbb{Q})
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+sheaf"} constant sheaf
            of rational numbers on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em lower real number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sh}(X)
            is then defined as a subsheaf of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(\mathbb{Q})
            satisfying the axioms above (interpreted in the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi sup
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto \sup U_x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            (taken as a subset of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
          %p
            Conversely, a lower semicontinuous function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to \mathbb{R} \cup \{ +\infty \}
            defines an internal lower real number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            with sections
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi φ
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(A) \coloneqq \{ \varphi : A \to \mathbb{Q} | \forall x \in A: \varphi(x) \lt f(x) \} \subseteq \Delta(\mathbb{Q})(A)
          %p
            over open sets
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq X
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "#Mulvey1974"} Mulvey (1974, page 28)
            for details.
          %p
            For the externally constructive version of this, it is best to take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            of lower real numbers in place of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \cup \{\infty\}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                D. Lesnik,
                %em Synthetic Topology and Constructive Metric Spaces
                , PhD University of Ljubljana 2010. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.fmf.uni-lj.si/storage/19160/PhD_Davorin.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p#Mulvey1974
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Mulvey"} C. Mulvey
                (1974):
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Intuitionistic Algebra and Representations of Rings
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Recent Advances in the Representation Theory of Rings and C*-Algebras by Continuous Sections
            %li
              %p
                J. Z. Reichman,
                %em Semicontinuous Real Numbers in a Topos
                , JPAA
                %strong 28
                (1983) pp.81-91.
            %li
              %p
                Guillaume Raynaud,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibred Contextual Quantum Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://etheses.bham.ac.uk/id/eprint/1685/"} etheses:1685
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://etheses.bham.ac.uk//id/eprint/1685/1/Raynaud14PhD.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            See also the following MO-discussion: (
            %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/108029/simplification-in-semi-continuous-real?rq=1"}> link
            )
